{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I gave you empty stomachs [Bb]in all your [F]cities
[Dm]Lack of bread in all your [F]places, yet you re[C]fused
I with[Bb]held the [C]rain when [Dm]harvest was [Bb]near
Sent it on one [C]city, but not on an[Dm]other
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Fields staggered for water but [Bb]found no re[F]lief
[Dm]Blight and mildew struck your [F]gardens and [C]trees
[Bb]Locusts devou[F]red figs and vines [Dm]you [Bb]loved
Plagues went out as they [C]did to [Dm]Egypt
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Your young men killed by the [Dm]sword, horses taken
[Bb]Stench of camps rose into [F]your nos[C]trils
[Bb]I overthrew you like [Dm]Sodom and Gomorrah
A [Bb]charred stick [C]snatched from the [Dm]fire
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]Yet you did [C]not return to me, [Dm]declares the Lord
There[Bb]fore I will do [C]this to you, Is[Dm]rael
Prepare yourself [C]to [Bb]meet your God, Israel
[C]He who forms [Dm]the [C]moun[Bb]tains and creates the wind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [C]LORD, the God of hosts, is his [Dm]name
{end_of_verse}

